Let's start by merging the square roots:

$\begin{align}
\sqrt{12}\cdot\sqrt{y^3}\cdot\sqrt{6y}
&=\sqrt{12\cdot y^3\cdot 6y}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{72y^4}
\end{align}$

Now we remove all perfect squares from inside the square root:

$\begin{align}
\sqrt{72y^4}
&=\sqrt{6^2\cdot 2\cdot \left(y^2\right)^2}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{6^2}\cdot\sqrt{2}\cdot\sqrt{ \left(y^2\right)^2}
\\\\
&=6\cdot \sqrt{2}\cdot y^2
\\\\
&=6y^2\sqrt{2}
\end{align}$
